WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.755
Open WebUI is a web interface for interacting with local and remote AI models.

00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:08.260
It gives users a familiar chat-based workspace where they can ask questions,

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.700
compare models, manage conversations, upload supporting material,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.558
and organize AI-assisted workflows.

00:00:13.558 --> 00:00:16.320
In a homelab, small team, or private AI environment,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.310
it often becomes the visible layer that turns model infrastructure into something people

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.180
can actually use.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.135
It is important to separate the web interface from the model runtime.

00:00:24.135 --> 00:00:25.980
A runtime loads and serves models.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.955
A web UI provides the user-facing experience: accounts, conversations, settings, prompts,

00:00:30.955 --> 00:00:33.630
document workflows, model selection, and administration.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:37.595
Open WebUI may connect to local inference services, remote APIs,

00:00:37.595 --> 00:00:41.600
or OpenAI-compatible endpoints at a high level, but it is not the model itself.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.735
A web UI adds usability and workflow structure, but it also adds administration concerns.

00:00:46.735 --> 00:00:48.055
Conversations may be stored.

00:00:48.055 --> 00:00:50.780
Uploaded files may become part of knowledge workflows.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.520
Users may have different permissions.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.100
Endpoint credentials may be configured in the application.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.860
Logs, backups, and browser access can all carry sensitive information.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.590
A chat interface feels simple, but it sits on top of real systems and real data.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.620
Avoid the assumption that local automatically means secure.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:09.935
A local or private AI stack can improve privacy compared with sending everything to a

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:10.660
public service,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.740
but only if access is controlled, deployment choices are deliberate,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.260
and data handling is understood.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.500
Open WebUI is most useful when it is treated as a manageable AI workspace,

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.170
not just a convenient front end.
